{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {Consider an FIR \{h}{\fs16 \dn6 
m}{, m=0,...M\} of length M+1 with M even.
 Temporarily define the sequence \{g}{\fs16 
\dn6 m}{=h}{\fs16 \dn6 m-M/2}{, m=-M/2,...,M/2\}.
 For \{g}{\fs16 \dn6 m}{\} (i) even, (ii)
 odd, and (iii) neither even or odd, compute
 the FR of the corresponding FIRs \{h}{\fs16 
\dn6 m}{\} using the DFT to approximate 
the DTFT and plot the magnitude and phase.
 Comment especially upon the nature of the
 phase.}}
}
.TXT 14 0 54 0
Cg a61.375000,62.000000,137
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {For each of the FIRs you considered,
 write down the ZT and plot its poles and
 zeros. comment especially upon the nature
 of the zeros.}}
}
